# The plugin's `targets` file: one line for each iterate mind to lend this Herdr to, as itx.<name>
# (default jonas.herdr):
#
#   <the mind's address>  [name]  [key]
#
# The address is the mind's domain, as in `iterate login <address>`. The bridge uses this computer's
# own sign-in to the mind: sign in once with `iterate login <address>`.
#
# A line that ends in `key` gives its bridge a key of its own instead, kept in
# "<config dir>/keys/<address>.key" (mode 600). It may lend the one name and add events under the
# stream's folder, and nothing else. A member of the mind allows it once: the plugin shows a
# notification, and the link is in the state dir's "<address>.allow-link".
example.com
